BOOK:Static Loads
NUMBER: 7 CONDITION: Self_weight_Beam
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: If this condition is applied to beams, a load is calculated and assigned, depending on the self-weight of the material, the area of the section and the direction of the gravity.
QUESTION: Self_weight_load#CB#(.)
VALUE: -
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 8 CONDITION: Global_Beam_Load
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: A static pressure load over the beam given in global axes. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m) for the beam pressures.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 9 CONDITION: Global_Projected_Beam_Load
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: A static pressure load over the beam given in global axes and projected as if the length of the beam was the projected length over the pressure vector. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m) for the beam pressures.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 10 CONDITION: Local_Beam_Load
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: A static pressure load over the beam given in the same local axes used to define the section. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m) for the beam pressures.\n\t (N*m/m) for the beam distributed momentum.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: Local_X_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Local_Y_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Local_Z_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Local_Mx_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
