NUMBER: 17 CONDITION: Beam_Temperature
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This condition considers the deformation supported by the beam when there is a uniform temperature change in all the beam.
QUESTION: alpha
VALUE: 0.000012
QUESTION: Delta_T(Degrees_Celsius)
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 18 CONDITION: Shell_triangular_face_Load
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: This load is similar to that of 'Shell_Face_Load' but its intensity changes depending on the point where it is applied. The two points define an imaginary line in the space. For every point of the geometry line  where the load is applied, it is possible to project this point on the imaginary line and interpolate the values related to these points depending on where it is projected. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the points\n\t(N/m) for the pressures.
TITLE: Position
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_point_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_point_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_point_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: X_point_2
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_point_2
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_point_2
VALUE: 0.0
TITLE: Pressures
