BOOK:General properties
NUMBER: 26 CONDITION: Section
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This property must be assigned to beams with arbitrary shape section. 'Inertia y' is the inertia modulus related to the Y' local axe. 'Inertia z' is the inertia modulus related to the Z' local axe. J is the torsion inertia. E is the Young Modulus and G is the Torsion modulus. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m2) for the area\n\t(m4) for the inertias and J\n\t(N/m2) for 'E' and 'G'\n\t(N/m3) for the Specific_weight.
TITLE: Data
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-Default-,-Automatic-,-Automatic_alt-)
VALUE: -Automatic-
HELP: Local axes are used to define the orientation of the section. After analysis, results will be displayed related to these local axes system.\nIn this system, Local X' axe must have the same direction than the beam. If option 'Automatic' is used, they can be viewed, after assigned, with button 'draw'. It is possible also to create user defined local axes systems. All local axes systems can be viewed, after analysis, in the postprocessing part.
QUESTION: Name
VALUE: -
STATE: HIDDEN
