NUMBER: 27 CONDITION: Rectangular_Section
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This property must be assigned to beams with rectangular section. 'Width y' is the width in the Y' local axe direction. 'Width z' is the width in the Z' local axe direction. E is the Young Modulus and G is the Torsion modulus. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the widths\n\t(N/m2) for 'E' and 'G'\n\t(N/m3) for the Specific_weight.
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-Default-,-Automatic-,-Automatic_alt-)
VALUE: -Automatic-
HELP: Local axes are used to define the orientation of the section. After analysis, results will be displayed related to these local axes system.\nIn this system, Local X' axe must have the same direction than the beam. If option 'Automatic' is used, they can be viewed, after assigned, with button 'draw'. It is possible also to create user defined local axes systems. All local axes systems can be viewed, after analysis, in the postprocessing part.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: Width_y
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Width_z
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: G
VALUE: 8.1e10
QUESTION: E
VALUE: 2.1e11
QUESTION: Specific_weight
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 28 CONDITION: Shell
