VALUE: 0
QUESTION: Disconnect_z_rotation#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 36 CONDITION: Line_disconnect_degrees
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
CANREPEAT: yes
HELP: To disconnect some degrees in all points over one line, select the degrees to disconnect and give an Identifier. Then, assign the same identifier using condition 'Disconnect_Id' to all the beam or shell elements that must form a rigid group disconnected from the node.\nValue -ANY- means that all the elements around the node will form independent groups will their degrees disconnected.\nExample: if the 3 rotations are marked in the nodes of one line with identifier 'Id1', and the same identifier 'Id1' is assigned to several shell elements that are over this node then, these shell elements will be rigid between them and will rotate freely related to the rest or beams or shell elements.
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to disconnect is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and disconnect the degrees related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
